    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">20 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Two pointers</span><span class=\"chip accent\">In-place compaction</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/remove-duplicates-from-sorted-array-ii/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 80</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array II</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Look two slots back in what you have KEPT, not in the input: a value may be written unless it equals <code>nums[k-2]</code>. One read pointer, one write pointer, one pass: O(n) time, O(1) space, and the same line with <code>k-m</code> handles \"at most m copies\".</p>\n"
